Before use: verify exact physical stocks, remaining quantities, labels/basis, homogeneity, balance suitability and handling/safety review. Ambrox stock is the recorded 25% w/w 3/7/0.5/1.5 g product/DPG/IPM/ethanol mixture. Orris is current 9% w/w supplied PW product in DEP, NOT 9% irones.

PLANNED, not existing: Coumarin 20% w/w DEP from a logged 2.000+8.000 g preparation; Heliotropal 10% w/w DEP from 1.000+9.000 g. Both require usable homogeneous solutions. Do not substitute existing unknown-basis Coumarin, saturated DPG Coumarin, or Heliotropin Fleuressence.

Smallest master transfer 20 mg: for a 1% weighing-uncertainty objective require verified uncertainty at most 0.2 mg or scale the whole master. A 0.001 g display does not establish this. No raw microlitre amounts are authorized.

Carrier check: DEP 698 mg; DPG 837.5 mg; TEC 800 mg; IPM 21.25 mg; ethanol 63.75 mg. No arbitrary extra solvent to repair a weighing deviation.

Full rationale, exact lineage, comparisons and both verbatim analyses: formulas/Prada_LHomme_Intense_Astra_V2_30mL_EDP.md. Canonical design accounting: docs/research/Prada_LHomme_Intense_Astra_V2_accounting.json. All diagnostic-volume numbers belong to the model projection only.
